# SPA fallback: this is a React Router app — every route needs to resolve to
# index.html so client-side routing can take over, otherwise a direct link or
# an F5 on any route other than "/" (e.g. /render, /planta-humanizada) 404s.
#
# NOTE: /api/*, /results/* and /uploads/* are NOT proxied here yet — the
# backend isn't hosted anywhere publicly reachable yet. Once it is, add rules
# like the ones already sketched in frontend/netlify.toml (or right here,
# since _redirects wins on a plain drag-and-drop deploy where netlify.toml
# isn't read) pointing at the backend's real URL, before those rules are
# needed for the app to actually work end-to-end.
/*   /index.html   200
